<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 3.05 trln lira of 2-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 3.05 trln lira of 2-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish Treasury sold 3.05 trillion lira of two-year, inflation-indexed, three-month coupon payment bonds on Tuesday, down sharply from the 198.1 trillion lira worth of similar bonds it sold at its June 3 auction at the same risk premium.</p>
<p>    Amount	: 3.05 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Risk premium: 32 percent</p>
<p>    Total bids  : 27 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Maturity    : June 18, 1999</p>
<p>Value date  : June 18, 1997</p>
<p>The central bank has 43.4 trillion lira of reverse repo repayments due on Wednesday when banks will pay three trillion lira for today's auction.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
